title: Dashboard › Filters › Date range shortcuts, keys and the address
route: /dashboard?from=2026-10-14&to=2026-10-20
intro: The faster ways through the calendar: four shortcuts that apply at once, the month arrows, the keyboard, and how the range is written to and read from the address. Today in the demo is Tue 20 Oct 2026.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Calendar pop-up is open\nShortcuts at the left"

group gPre "Shortcuts (each ends today and applies at once)"
  click c1 "Click 'Last 7 days'\nOct 14 – Oct 20, 2026"
  click c2 "Click 'Last 30 days'\nSep 21 – Oct 20, 2026 (the default)"
  click c3 "Click 'Last 90 days'\nJul 23 – Oct 20, 2026"
  click c4 "Click 'This month'\nOct 1 – Oct 20, 2026"
endgroup
process p1 "Range saved and the calendar closes\nNo Apply needed"

group gNav "Moving around the calendar"
  click n1 "Click the left arrow 'Earlier months'\nThe two months move back one"
  click n2 "Click the right arrow 'Later months'\nThe two months move forward one"
  decision nd "Does the month after the right one start after today?"
  process n3 "Right arrow is dimmed and disabled"
  process n4 "Months move"
  click k1 "Press ArrowLeft, ArrowRight, ArrowUp or ArrowDown on a day\nMoves the focus by 1 or 7 days"
  process k2 "Focus stops at today; the months scroll to keep the day in view"
  click k3 "Press Enter or Space on the focused day\nSame as clicking it"
endgroup

group gUrl "The address"
  decision u1 "Is the applied range the default Sep 21 – Oct 20?"
  process u2 "No from or to in the address"
  process u3 "?from=2026-10-14&to=2026-10-20 added"
  start u4 "Open a link that has from and to"
  decision u5 "Are from and to real dates, with from not after to?"
  process u6 "Range applied from the link"
  process u7 "Ignored: the remembered range stays"
  start u8 "Open an old link with ?period=7d, 30d or quarter"
  process u9 "Mapped to the last 7, 30 or 90 days ending Oct 20"
endgroup

store w1 "Filter 'range'"
screen sc "Date button shows the range\nGreen and bold when it is not the default\nOne day shows as 'Oct 10, 2026'"
process p2 "Payers at a glance rescales: 'Denied (N d)' and 'Info asks (N d)' use N days, N = days in the range"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Pick a date range"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Clear filters and empty states"

s1 --> c1 & c2 & c3 & c4
c1 & c2 & c3 & c4 --> p1 --> w1
s1 --> n1 & n2 & k1
n1 --> n4
n2 --> nd
nd -->|Yes| n3
nd -->|No| n4
k1 --> k2 --> k3
k3 -.-> g1
w1 --> u1
u1 -->|Yes| u2 --> sc
u1 -->|No| u3 --> sc
u4 --> u5
u5 -->|Yes| u6 --> w1
u5 -->|No| u7 --> sc
u8 --> u9 --> w1
sc --> p2
sc -.-> g2
